		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: turn off Voice Prompts?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2570&amp;p=21242#p21242"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>BTW,  noticed that you can select Radio below the option "Use Voice Prompt memory" in the CPS "Download Callsign database"<br>I couldn't find RT3S/MD-UV380 in that list.</div></blockquote>This needs to be tidied up. I think its probably redundant, as the CPS now normally asks the firmware what type of radio it is, for most operations.<br><br>But a lot of people still run old quite old firmware which does not support reading the radio type <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_sad.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":-(" title="Sad"><br><br>BTW.<br><br>The reason that Voice Prompts default to on, is because otherwise blind users would be unable to use the radio after loading the Voice Prompts, as they would have no way to get to the menu to enable the prompts<br><br>Generally, once you turn off the VP they won't come back on unless you reset the settings or occasionaly on firmware updates the settings need to be cleared when new features are added or redundant settings are removed.<br><br>So its normally not a big problem<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sun Jan 08, 2023 6:41 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
